WEBVTT

00:13.847 --> 00:18.351
Those who ceaselessly hone
their killing arts are known as "Masters."

00:18.810 --> 00:23.773
After many generations,
they have gained lethal abilities

00:23.857 --> 00:26.359
called "Modified Bloodlines."

00:27.027 --> 00:32.323
This is the story of one such Master,
the Poison Master, Hikaru Gero,

00:32.699 --> 00:35.243
and his attempts to get married.

00:43.752 --> 00:47.213
Locked in Latata

00:47.297 --> 00:50.884
Secrets in my veins Latata

00:50.967 --> 00:52.677
I know you want it

00:52.761 --> 00:54.471
And sure, I love it

00:54.554 --> 00:58.725
So I stay behind the mask Latata

00:58.808 --> 01:02.062
Run, run, run back to back Run

01:02.145 --> 01:05.940
Fun, fun, fun unpredictable but fun

01:06.024 --> 01:08.151
At the end of every mind game

01:08.234 --> 01:12.113
Shoot through the darkened night

01:12.197 --> 01:15.325
Poisoned in our bodies still

01:15.408 --> 01:19.996
Laugh at us our reckless souls

01:20.080 --> 01:21.331
TOXIC

01:21.414 --> 01:23.625
For you I will

01:23.708 --> 01:24.918
TOXIC

01:25.001 --> 01:27.337
Rewrite my destiny

01:27.420 --> 01:30.840
Losing it, falling for you

01:30.924 --> 01:34.302
What's tomorrow Kill or Kiss

01:34.385 --> 01:35.512
TOXIC

01:35.595 --> 01:37.847
Tell me what you want

01:37.931 --> 01:39.098
TOXIC

01:39.182 --> 01:41.392
I'll stay right here

01:41.476 --> 01:44.854
Like a spell, I'll be by your side

01:44.938 --> 01:48.608
What you gonna do Kill or Kiss

01:52.529 --> 01:55.115
Kill or Kiss

01:56.199 --> 01:58.660
Kill or Kiss

01:59.744 --> 02:01.996
Kill or Kiss

02:08.086 --> 02:09.420
Remember, Gero:

02:09.504 --> 02:11.548
The key is to size up your target.

02:11.631 --> 02:14.175
Assess the machine,
the prize's position,

02:14.259 --> 02:18.972
the strength of the arm,
and so on. And then...

02:19.931 --> 02:20.849
Strike your prey!

02:22.142 --> 02:23.309
There's a lot to it.

02:24.686 --> 02:26.980
Now, you try it!

02:27.063 --> 02:29.732
A crane game is an old standby for dates.

02:29.816 --> 02:32.026
Pull it off effortlessly
and score big.

02:32.110 --> 02:34.237
Ya gotta keep doing things
to win her over.

02:34.320 --> 02:35.738
Strike my prey.

02:42.453 --> 02:43.788
I blew through 10,000 yen.

02:44.038 --> 02:46.666
Might be better to avoid these
till you get the hang of it.

02:46.749 --> 02:47.959
It's easy to get stuck.

02:51.087 --> 02:52.797
I bet I could handle that one.

02:54.883 --> 02:56.301
How's this?

02:56.551 --> 03:00.889
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow.

03:01.139 --> 03:02.557
Spotted garden eels.

03:03.433 --> 03:04.142
Finished!

03:04.392 --> 03:07.478
Perfect! You are No. 1!

03:07.562 --> 03:08.897
Congratulations!

03:08.980 --> 03:10.773
That was incredible.

03:11.524 --> 03:13.401
But it might not win girls.

03:15.153 --> 03:16.154
Next thing!

03:18.114 --> 03:19.073
Next thing.

03:21.117 --> 03:22.368
That's beyond niche.

03:23.119 --> 03:26.497
Let's make hunting memories
that'll last a lifetime.

03:29.584 --> 03:31.753
By the way, Gero, have you heard?

03:33.129 --> 03:34.297
About the "Hitman Hunter."

03:36.132 --> 03:39.510
You mean the string of famous killers
getting taken out?

03:40.345 --> 03:43.806
The "Hunter's" goals and identity
are a mystery, but skills? Proven.

03:44.641 --> 03:48.436
Dan the Dismemberer and Kushima
the Spear Master got taken down.

03:49.062 --> 03:50.939
Masters are the best assassins out there.

03:51.231 --> 03:54.776
I doubt many people could take the
Spear Master in a fight, in particular.

03:55.610 --> 03:57.528
You'd better watch out, too.

03:57.612 --> 03:58.529
Right.

03:58.905 --> 04:00.573
Okay, all done.

04:00.657 --> 04:01.449
Check it out.

04:02.408 --> 04:04.202
Is this really supposed to be fun?

04:04.535 --> 04:06.496
No one likes a downer.

04:08.289 --> 04:09.874
I take it back.

04:10.208 --> 04:12.252
It's a memory, Gero.

04:12.877 --> 04:15.880
A reminder that we had fun together.

04:16.297 --> 04:18.258
Is that how it works?

04:19.300 --> 04:24.264
You'd be happy if a girl got into talking
about DIY candy kits with you, right?

04:24.806 --> 04:25.932
Well, yeah.

04:26.724 --> 04:28.685
I'm not saying to force yourself,

04:29.102 --> 04:32.272
but if you can get caught up
in something your date enjoys,

04:32.355 --> 04:35.358
nothing beats that.

04:39.862 --> 04:41.447
Want to call it a day...

04:49.956 --> 04:51.040
Hikaru Gero.

04:51.124 --> 04:52.667
We need to talk.

04:53.668 --> 04:56.379
But first...

04:56.754 --> 04:58.548
Take a picture with me, too.

05:00.133 --> 05:00.758
Huh?

05:04.637 --> 05:07.390
So, uh, Kimie Arashiyama.

05:07.473 --> 05:11.853
You want to hire Gero, and
you've been looking for a chance to talk?

05:13.187 --> 05:15.273
You could've reached out
on the Dark Nav.

05:16.482 --> 05:19.986
A beauty like me comes around once in
ten million years, and I'm here for you.

05:20.778 --> 05:22.697
You've gotta be over the moon.

05:25.658 --> 05:26.659
Let's call it a day, Gero.

05:26.743 --> 05:30.204
Hey, hang on! Wait! I'm sorry!
At least hear me out!

05:31.122 --> 05:35.501
Shadowing the guy you want to hire
doesn't exactly inspire trust.

05:35.585 --> 05:37.628
You're right. I'm sorry.

05:38.421 --> 05:42.425
I thought the Hitman Hunter had come
to get Gero for a minute there.

05:42.508 --> 05:44.469
Oh, yeah, about that.

05:46.054 --> 05:48.473
The thing is, I'm a Master, too.

05:49.265 --> 05:50.391
Hikaru Gero.

05:50.475 --> 05:53.644
Until someone takes care
of the Hitman Hunter,

05:53.728 --> 05:55.021
I'll let you...

05:55.980 --> 05:57.482
protect me!

05:57.565 --> 05:58.733
Come on. Let's go.

05:59.358 --> 06:00.234
Wait, wait, wait!

06:00.985 --> 06:04.489
Anyway, shouldn't a Master
be able to protect herself?

06:04.572 --> 06:08.201
F-Fighting's not really my thing!

06:08.493 --> 06:10.453
Let's hear her out a little longer.

06:12.663 --> 06:15.208
What? But...

06:15.500 --> 06:19.670
If a Master is asking for help
from a family she has no ties to,

06:19.754 --> 06:21.839
she must be in a pretty bad spot.

06:23.591 --> 06:25.843
Right, Arashiyama?

06:26.094 --> 06:28.846
Arashiyama. Arashiyama. Arashiyama.

06:31.599 --> 06:32.433
H-Hey!

06:37.105 --> 06:39.857
Is Master Hikaru seriously
being this nice to me?

06:39.941 --> 06:46.030
And is he holding me in his arms
and calling my name right now?

06:46.364 --> 06:47.824
He's paying attention to me?

06:48.449 --> 06:51.994
My mind went blank when I found out
the Hitman Hunter was after me,

06:52.078 --> 06:54.539
but how lucky am I to meet
the Master Hikaru Gero?

06:54.622 --> 06:57.667
I don't even have an appointment.
It's gotta be a nuisance.

06:57.750 --> 07:00.753
But he's still treating me so courteously.

07:01.212 --> 07:02.338
Arashiyama.

07:04.841 --> 07:06.217
Arashiyama?

07:09.303 --> 07:11.389
I'm getting beyond the royal treatment.

07:12.932 --> 07:14.600
- What's this?
- A lover's spat?

07:14.684 --> 07:15.935
- A cheat?
- A love triangle?

07:16.018 --> 07:19.147
Now I'm safe for sure!

07:19.230 --> 07:21.941
Come try me, Hitman Hunter!

07:22.024 --> 07:23.025
Wait.

07:23.651 --> 07:26.070
I d-didn't say I'd take the job yet.

07:26.529 --> 07:28.322
Talk about a hearty laugh.

07:29.991 --> 07:32.243
I'll make an exception and show you...

07:32.618 --> 07:34.871
just what kind of Master I am.

07:40.626 --> 07:43.171
- It's that table again.
- Don't look. Just ignore them.

07:50.219 --> 07:51.262
Ham!

07:52.180 --> 07:53.264
Let's start over.

07:53.639 --> 07:56.684
I'm Kimie Arashiyama, the Hamster Master.

07:56.767 --> 07:58.895
This is my partner, Sirius.

07:59.562 --> 08:03.524
Hikaru Gero, he's the one
who found you in town.

08:04.734 --> 08:08.196
When it comes to intel-gathering
and small, fiddly stuff, I'm your woman.

08:08.279 --> 08:11.157
At least as long as I have
these little guys helping me.

08:11.240 --> 08:13.034
He's adorable!

08:13.451 --> 08:14.243
Ham.

08:14.577 --> 08:15.620
Ham.

08:15.703 --> 08:17.705
So you're related to the Beast Clan.

08:18.039 --> 08:23.628
Masters are all expert killers,
but not necessarily good fighters.

08:24.045 --> 08:26.964
Technically, I'm more about
assassination and traps myself.

08:27.423 --> 08:30.092
All that, and you're still
not a "good fighter"?

08:30.510 --> 08:33.596
I don't want anything to do
with the Hitman Hunter,

08:34.138 --> 08:40.102
but the association I'm part of
is all fired up to take the jerk out.

08:40.186 --> 08:42.396
And you're in danger,
so you want a bodyguard?

08:42.480 --> 08:43.481
You got it.

08:44.148 --> 08:48.027
If you're in an association of clans,
just get one of them to protect...

08:48.110 --> 08:49.529
No chance of that.

08:51.239 --> 08:54.325
Up until my great-great-grandpa's
generation, we were Rat Masters.

08:54.408 --> 08:58.829
Even the main Beast Clan respected us,
so we got to throw our weight around.

08:59.330 --> 09:01.332
Now, though, our bloodline's thinned out,

09:01.415 --> 09:06.462
and I wouldn't be surprised if we got
stripped of our Master title tomorrow.

09:08.047 --> 09:11.092
Me, I've never even killed anybody.

09:11.175 --> 09:13.719
This collar's the only link I have left.

09:13.803 --> 09:16.430
All the branches of the Beast Clan
have to wear them.

09:17.139 --> 09:19.100
So you see how it is.

09:20.142 --> 09:22.687
I show up to association meetings
when they tell me to,

09:22.770 --> 09:25.815
but they've already decided
the important stuff without me.

09:25.898 --> 09:27.984
Like this plan to take on the Hunter.

09:28.734 --> 09:30.486
They said to my face:

09:31.028 --> 09:33.239
"A 'Master' who can't and doesn't kill,

09:33.489 --> 09:36.659
and who works a normal job
at a normal company,"

09:36.742 --> 09:39.996
should at least make herself useful
as a shield."

09:43.207 --> 09:44.709
Thanks for today.

09:45.209 --> 09:46.419
I feel calmer now.

09:47.628 --> 09:51.465
I got carried away earlier, but the future
head of one of the Five Great Families

09:51.549 --> 09:54.218
wouldn't guard a branch-family nobody
in a million years.

09:54.802 --> 09:57.513
I can't afford your massive fee,
for one thing.

09:59.056 --> 10:01.601
I'm so glad I got to meet my fave
before I die.

10:02.685 --> 10:04.270
Let's say 10,000 yen a day.

10:05.396 --> 10:07.023
When should I start guarding you?

10:07.106 --> 10:08.983
Are you sure, Gero?

10:10.318 --> 10:11.110
I mean...

10:12.361 --> 10:15.615
You're in a real bind,
aren't you, Arashiyama?

10:18.784 --> 10:20.745
Well, I don't see a problem.

10:21.203 --> 10:23.873
This wasn't part of my plan
to get you hitched.

10:23.956 --> 10:27.752
Still, you sure are honing
that charm of yours. Good job.

10:32.214 --> 10:34.383
It's like he's acting out my fantasies.

10:34.467 --> 10:36.385
Kinosaki, what should I do?

10:36.469 --> 10:38.387
Try hugging her back.

10:38.471 --> 10:40.514
Huh? You know I can't!

10:44.810 --> 10:46.395
Oh, there you are.

10:46.479 --> 10:47.605
- Ham!
- Hey.

10:47.688 --> 10:52.401
Hikaru Gero and assistant! I'm gonna
introduce you to the association today.

10:52.485 --> 10:53.527
Ham!

10:53.819 --> 10:56.155
Like it or not,
you'll have to deal with them.

10:57.198 --> 10:59.784
So this is how Arashiyama normally acts?

11:00.242 --> 11:03.037
She's the quirkiest woman so far,

11:03.204 --> 11:05.039
but she is a fellow Master.

11:05.122 --> 11:08.501
Maybe someone like her
will mesh with Gero better than I think.

11:11.087 --> 11:12.129
This is the place.

11:12.880 --> 11:14.215
I'll do the introductions.

11:14.924 --> 11:16.509
Serpent Master, Ryumon.

11:16.592 --> 11:18.761
Owl Master, Chojabaru.

11:18.844 --> 11:20.763
Hippo Master, Shibaseki.

11:20.846 --> 11:22.848
Orca Master, Kankaiji.

11:23.140 --> 11:24.850
Buffalo Master, Horita.

11:25.101 --> 11:26.852
Alligator Master, Hamawaki.

11:30.898 --> 11:32.441
Is everybody napping?

11:32.525 --> 11:34.568
No, the humans...

11:35.403 --> 11:36.946
are all dead.

11:45.913 --> 11:48.499
Are you in the association, too?
What happened?

11:49.375 --> 11:50.126
Who's that?

11:51.919 --> 11:53.963
Kinosaki! Arashiyama! Run!

12:02.263 --> 12:03.180
Um...

12:03.264 --> 12:06.767
You're a Poison Master, aren't you?

12:07.143 --> 12:09.895
I don't know what you're doing here,

12:10.980 --> 12:12.565
but this is perfect timing.

12:13.107 --> 12:15.276
Now I don't have to go look for you.

12:15.985 --> 12:19.488
And I can cross a big name off my list.

12:22.032 --> 12:23.993
(The Hitman Hunter)

12:25.035 --> 12:25.870
Did...

12:27.371 --> 12:28.497
Did he just...

12:28.831 --> 12:29.999
stab him?

12:30.082 --> 12:31.167
Hey.

12:31.625 --> 12:33.544
Run. Now.

12:38.340 --> 12:40.801
I avoided a fatal cut by a hair.

12:41.177 --> 12:43.471
I've stopped the bleeding,
but it won't last.

12:44.430 --> 12:46.515
You the Hitman Hunter?

12:46.807 --> 12:48.350
What are you after?

13:03.365 --> 13:04.450
He did that...

13:04.992 --> 13:06.702
with one little knife?

13:07.077 --> 13:08.787
This guy's not human.

13:23.177 --> 13:25.095
I'm in trouble if this drags out.

13:25.179 --> 13:28.057
Can I hold out and set a trap
for him? No chance.

13:28.641 --> 13:30.768
I've just gotta face him head-on,

13:31.352 --> 13:33.062
and go all out from the start.

13:34.647 --> 13:36.857
Optical reflex accelerator.

13:36.941 --> 13:38.692
Toxin: Vision.

13:39.109 --> 13:41.237
Muscle reflex enhancer.

13:41.320 --> 13:43.197
Toxin: Javelin Strike.

13:45.824 --> 13:48.118
I'll overwhelm him with a double dose.

14:14.228 --> 14:15.396
What's up?

14:15.479 --> 14:17.606
Huh? A mistake?

14:18.399 --> 14:20.484
Yeah. Okay.

14:20.818 --> 14:23.988
But the Poison Master's
still a hitman, right?

14:24.947 --> 14:27.366
He takes bodyguard gigs on the Dark Nav?

14:27.700 --> 14:29.785
Are you sure you've got the right guy?

14:30.369 --> 14:33.163
No one in the Five Great Families
works gigs like that.

14:33.664 --> 14:38.544
And he seems dangerous.
He shot two syringes into his own neck.

14:38.836 --> 14:43.549
Yeah, two at once. Dangerous, right?

14:44.675 --> 14:47.303
I think I'd better take care
of him now after all.

14:47.928 --> 14:48.929
Yeah.

14:51.515 --> 14:53.183
I'll beat him to the punch.

15:20.044 --> 15:20.836
No way.

15:21.128 --> 15:23.547
I took Toxin: Vision,
and I still can't keep track of him?

15:24.590 --> 15:26.050
That was a close one.

15:29.136 --> 15:30.346
You guys okay?

15:30.638 --> 15:32.973
(You'd better believe it)

15:35.684 --> 15:37.853
You sure are nice to the animals.

15:39.146 --> 15:41.649
Did they do anything wrong?

15:41.982 --> 15:45.986
Where did you come from?
A branch of the Iron Clan?

15:46.445 --> 15:49.239
I'm just a regular guy.

15:49.949 --> 15:52.034
No way. You must be from some family.

15:52.117 --> 15:55.162
I don't need to lie to someone
who's about to die.

15:56.580 --> 15:59.708
All my relatives are teachers.

16:02.378 --> 16:03.504
Then...

16:04.630 --> 16:06.090
He's a mutant.

16:06.966 --> 16:10.094
Masters spend generations
building up their bloodlines,

16:10.511 --> 16:13.430
and this freak has surpassed them in one.

16:13.806 --> 16:16.934
Damn it. I've never tried this before,

16:17.267 --> 16:18.435
but what choice do I have?

16:19.353 --> 16:21.397
Toxin: Triple Dose.

16:22.898 --> 16:25.943
U-Um, why would you do that?

16:26.193 --> 16:27.736
It's suicide.

16:30.948 --> 16:34.743
I guess I should've known a triple dose...

16:35.619 --> 16:38.414
was more than I could take while injured.

16:39.039 --> 16:40.624
What did I tell you?

16:41.583 --> 16:46.964
This is what you get for killing
lots of people and spreading hatred.

16:49.758 --> 16:51.010
Please die.

16:54.513 --> 16:55.806
Promise me.

16:57.725 --> 17:00.561
Don't touch the two of...

17:10.237 --> 17:12.114
Hitman Hunter!

17:13.574 --> 17:15.492
You won't kill Hikaru Gero on my watch!

17:15.576 --> 17:17.244
Huh? Arashiyama?

17:17.619 --> 17:20.914
What? If you get in the way,
I've gotta "take care" of you, too.

17:20.998 --> 17:22.875
Shove it, you big dummy!

17:24.209 --> 17:27.671
"Spreading hatred" my ass!

17:28.130 --> 17:32.259
He offered to be my bodyguard!

17:32.342 --> 17:33.218
Ham!

17:33.302 --> 17:36.096
I'd rather die than be a shield
for some jerk,

17:36.430 --> 17:39.058
but I'm happy to die for my fave!

17:41.393 --> 17:42.519
Sirius Squad!

17:48.984 --> 17:50.444
Ham!

17:52.738 --> 17:53.906
Let's go.

17:54.990 --> 18:00.496
Modified Bloodline++: Canis Major!

18:00.829 --> 18:03.540
The Greater Dog that shines...

18:04.625 --> 18:06.126
in the winter sky!

18:06.210 --> 18:07.336
How do you like that?

18:15.594 --> 18:17.513
H-Hang on! What are you doing?

18:17.596 --> 18:18.972
What do you mean?

18:19.306 --> 18:22.392
I'm taking him to a doctor.
He's at death's door.

18:22.476 --> 18:23.143
Huh?

18:23.227 --> 18:25.354
Canis Major gave him a change of heart?

18:25.979 --> 18:28.107
Didn't you come to kill me?

18:28.190 --> 18:29.858
Why save my life?

18:32.319 --> 18:36.615
I've never seen Masters try to cover
for each other before.

18:37.032 --> 18:38.659
I don't want to kill you anymore.

18:39.201 --> 18:40.619
Isn't that...

18:40.869 --> 18:42.162
enough of a reason?

18:44.414 --> 18:45.541
I see.

18:46.625 --> 18:47.835
Put me down.

18:47.918 --> 18:48.877
But the doctor...

18:48.961 --> 18:51.255
This isn't so bad
that I can't fix it myself.

18:52.589 --> 18:55.008
My name's Piichi Nakagawa.

18:55.551 --> 18:57.886
I want to rest Master Hikaru's head
on my lap, too.

18:57.970 --> 18:59.596
My goal...

19:00.139 --> 19:04.309
is to wipe out the Beast Clan,
one of the Five Great Families.

19:04.393 --> 19:09.481
I heard they were planning "something
dangerous that'll kill a lot of people,"

19:09.731 --> 19:13.485
so I figured I'd take them out
before the damage could get too bad.

19:14.069 --> 19:16.989
Why did you hunt people
who weren't Beast Masters, then?

19:17.072 --> 19:18.115
They were just on the way.

19:18.198 --> 19:19.241
Come again?

19:19.741 --> 19:23.078
I had no clue
where to find the Beast Clan,

19:23.162 --> 19:25.914
so I went around asking people
who seemed to know them.

19:26.999 --> 19:30.752
A homicidal maniac
they did a deal with once.

19:30.836 --> 19:32.588
An old guy with a knife on a pole.

19:32.671 --> 19:35.007
People from their branch families.

19:35.549 --> 19:39.011
I took care of the dangerous ones
while I was at it.

19:39.303 --> 19:42.055
Oh. Wait, what?

19:42.389 --> 19:43.515
Dan the Dismemberer...

19:44.016 --> 19:48.687
took payment for killings
in octogenarian men instead of money.

19:49.563 --> 19:55.027
Kushima the Spear Master would involve
innocent bystanders to get his jobs done.

19:56.486 --> 20:00.032
I want to open a café with my girlfriend.

20:01.867 --> 20:06.496
But I've got to get rid of
all the dangerous people first,

20:07.831 --> 20:11.376
or our customers won't be able to relax.

20:12.878 --> 20:14.755
Why is his head still on her lap?

20:15.422 --> 20:18.800
You're picking a fight with one of
the Five Great Families? Are you nuts?

20:18.884 --> 20:23.639
Huh? But, uh, wouldn't it be better
if all the bad people were gone?

20:24.264 --> 20:27.100
Normally, that'd just be wishful thinking,

20:28.143 --> 20:30.979
but he might actually
be able to pull it off.

20:31.605 --> 20:36.109
I thought the Gero Family of Poison Masters
must be pretty dangerous, too.

20:36.485 --> 20:38.153
But it turns out you're different.

20:39.488 --> 20:44.243
You're not a threat to the world I want.

20:44.785 --> 20:47.329
At least, not right now.

20:47.996 --> 20:49.998
So, uh...

20:50.082 --> 20:51.833
You mean you're letting us go?

20:51.917 --> 20:52.751
Ham!

20:53.001 --> 20:55.128
Well, problem solved, then!

20:57.381 --> 21:03.011
Mr. Gero, do you know about the Beast Clan
through your family connections?

21:03.095 --> 21:04.596
Of course not.

21:05.305 --> 21:08.183
People call us the Five Great Families
for convenience,

21:08.267 --> 21:10.519
but it's not like we have much
to do with each other.

21:10.602 --> 21:12.229
Oh, I see.

21:13.772 --> 21:18.151
You're from a branch of the Beast Clan.
Do you know anything?

21:18.235 --> 21:20.946
I've never visited the main house
or met any of the family.

21:21.029 --> 21:22.030
That figures.

21:22.114 --> 21:25.742
All I know is I have this collar
they give all the branch fami...

21:28.578 --> 21:29.621
Arashiyama!

21:32.291 --> 21:33.500
A bat?

21:34.376 --> 21:36.253
Wh-What happened to Arashiyama?

21:36.545 --> 21:37.504
I don't know.

21:37.587 --> 21:39.381
Did this collar cause it?

21:39.464 --> 21:40.507
Whoa there.

21:40.590 --> 21:44.469
If you try to break that,
it'll suck the host's blood dry.

21:45.095 --> 21:49.516
The Bonda Constrictor is a living
accessory engineered to suck blood.

21:49.599 --> 21:54.313
I went ahead and activated it, meaning
that woman's got three days to live, tops.

21:55.022 --> 21:56.273
Why put that on her?

21:56.356 --> 21:58.608
Wouldn't want 'em
running off now, would I?

21:58.692 --> 22:00.444
The livestock, I mean.

22:02.195 --> 22:03.947
Don't give me that death glare.

22:04.031 --> 22:06.783
Hikaru Gero. Piichi Nakagawa.

22:06.867 --> 22:10.203
If you're looking for me,
I'll extend a special invitation to you.

22:10.996 --> 22:16.251
Come to the Beast Clan's home turf:
Dogo Animal Kingdom.

22:28.680 --> 22:30.891
Ah! Something smells fishy!

22:30.974 --> 22:32.809
I'm shocked, startled,
it's adding insult to injury

22:32.893 --> 22:34.144
I'm completely obsessed

22:34.227 --> 22:36.521
Ah! Something smells off!

22:36.605 --> 22:38.523
You're all bluff,
I'm sick and tired, so disappointed

22:38.607 --> 22:39.649
Bye-bye, mwah!

22:39.941 --> 22:42.694
It seems like I'm only good at

22:42.778 --> 22:45.530
workbooks for a child

22:45.614 --> 22:48.283
Even through infectious disease,
I want to love with you

22:48.366 --> 22:51.244
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

22:51.328 --> 22:53.747
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:53.830 --> 22:56.958
Darling, heading toward a twisted signpost

22:57.042 --> 22:59.461
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:59.544 --> 23:02.297
Just the two of us, consolation prize

23:12.557 --> 23:14.684
Ah, the scent of dance

23:14.768 --> 23:16.520
I'm completely obsessed

23:16.603 --> 23:17.938
with you as you flutter down

23:18.021 --> 23:20.190
Ah, something smells off

23:20.273 --> 23:22.400
I'm blown away by you

23:22.484 --> 23:23.401
Bye-bye, mwah!

23:23.485 --> 23:26.530
It seems like I'm only good at

23:26.613 --> 23:29.282
workbooks for a child

23:29.366 --> 23:32.119
I want us to share even our growing pains

23:32.202 --> 23:34.871
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

23:35.080 --> 23:37.582
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:37.666 --> 23:40.669
Darling, heading toward
a stagnant signpost

23:40.752 --> 23:43.255
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:43.338 --> 23:46.091
Singing a grand chorus cheekily

23:47.425 --> 23:49.469
Listening to you makes me sick.

23:49.553 --> 23:51.513
This is 100% a trap for sure!

23:51.596 --> 23:54.099
Absolutely delicious.

23:54.182 --> 23:56.893
Next time: "The Animal Kingdom."
